;">THE MOUSE THAT ROARED</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A consistent criticism levelled at Como is=
 that they are simply not =E2=80=9CItalian=E2=80=9D enough to be a bona fid=
e Serie A club. Bankrolled by an Indonesian ciggy manufacturer, their presi=
dent has helpfully likened their multi-hubbed business model to that of the=
 Walt Disney Company. In Cesc F=C3=A0bregas they have a Spanish coach and t=
heir starting XI against Lens in Bigger Cup on Wednesday didn=E2=80=99t fea=
ture a single Italian. To add insult to injury, they also thrashed their ho=
sts 9-1 in a show of outright vulgarity that will have had Serie A traditio=
nalists gesticulating angrily. Piling on the hurt against already-humiliate=
d opposition has never been the Italian way, unless both teams have formall=
y agreed to it before the game kicks off.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Still, if the Como squad was low on homegr=
own players, they certainly looked the part upon their arrival at Stade Bol=
laert-Delelis, stepping off their team coach and inspecting the pitch looki=
ng like an escape party from a Milan fashion week runway. Due in no small p=
art to the club=E2=80=99s official partnership with Rome=E2=80=99s haute co=
uture menswear house Brioni, F=C3=A0bregas and his globetrotting ensemble l=
ooked impossibly stylish in bespoke double-breasted suits, knitted cotton-s=
ilk-cashmere long-sleeve polos and soft slip-on nubuck loafers (sans socks,=
 of course), thoughtfully accessorised with designer shades even though it =
was already practically dark.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">While their pitch walk served as an ironic=
 counterweight to domestic football debate, once Como=E2=80=99s players had=
 swapped their designer duds for studs, they reverted to a brand of intense=
 front-foot football that couldn=E2=80=99t have been less <em>catenaccio</e=
m>, leaving their hapless French hosts chasing shadows. The <a href=3D"http=
s://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7=
fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPghQNuEAl_2n85-K0986DobAcybXy4PurKP8Kwk4B=
UVzNvez29fLxLxWF6t_9clmJNz93tr-LJE3qp7EUv6mffb1k3Mqb_vig-pWc1xoyDjzSOX57ejv=
QyOFPuWz3hdykvQZgkFVxhAT8vzA6-kNJ1URTckrJJystDIjqWDXKmu5gn8yFCJC4E92_r6lkUX=
rziBl32d9Ogfmdrvgz6rDYRm0OExnn_6ERV4550rs-W9eizEP3UOeadCyzWVrbqscx03p8XBCjk=
69Xip8Pb2JUB-A/4vh/2TM6KNhkR7i_7XGIm4wU_w/h28/h001.r99YWT5KUcyZ7ugT5gwUxgsj=
KNwQs6Een78tLhojLTI" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">9-1</a> [NINE =E2=80=93 Foot=
ball Daily Vidiprinter] victory was the biggest winning margin in Bigger Cu=
p history, with Como=E2=80=99s only dampener on their evening coming in the=
 form of a thunderous volley from Lens=E2=80=99 Ruben Aguilar. To make up f=
or this crushing disappointment, Como=E2=80=99s final two goals were scored=
 by Mattia Liberali and Matteo Papaccioli, a pair of teenage substitutes wh=
o could only have been more Italian if they=E2=80=99d celebrated by wheelin=
g away on a couple of Vespas.</p>
